From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent 9999998: an 'ap' section the controller never sent is not the controller's to delete

The autoconfiguration path deletes local 'ap' sections it never created, and on
the way there it also hands their section to a WSC M2 as if it were a free BSS
slot. Both are the same mistake: map-agent treats every mapagent 'ap' section as
controller-provisioned, when two producers write them.

There are two independent routes into the deletion, and both were live.

  handle_ap_autoconfig_wsc()            per WSC M2, per radio
    wifi_teardown_map_ifaces_by_radio() marks every 'ap' on the radio torndown
    the M2 loop                         clears the mark only on what the M2 sent
    wifi_clean_torndown_ifaces_on_radio()
      "multiap clean_stale_ifaces <ifname>"  ->  uci -q delete

  mlo_process_ap_mld_config()           per AP-MLD Config TLV
    step 1                              marks every 'ap' that carries an mld_id
    step 2                              re-affiliates only what the TLV listed
    wifi_clean_torndown_ifaces()        same deletion, no M2 needed

The victims are bhmld_ap_5 and bhmld_ap_6: the backhaul MLD bookkeeping
placeholders map_genconfig writes, with ifname='bhmld5'/'bhmld6', mld_id='3' and
the real radio in 'device'. They exist so that apmld_refresh_data_cb() runs
apmld_parse() for ap-mld-2 - it only iterates netif_aps whose cfg->mld_id equals
the MLD id - and they deliberately name an interface that is not a netdev, which
is why they are separate sections and not mld_id on wlan1-1/wlan2-1 (map-agent
989 and the note in map_genconfig). The controller has never heard of them. They
can therefore never survive a mark-and-sweep whose only un-marking rule is "the
controller sent it back".

Worse than the deletion, and measured on the running controller 2026-09-04: the
M2 handler does not always get as far as deleting a placeholder, because it
claims it first. wifi_get_first_available_ifname() returns the first torndown AP
on the radio, and on radio1 - which no longer had a legacy backhaul section to
absorb the backhaul M2 - that was bhmld_ap_5:

  mapagent.bhmld_ap_5.ssid='MAP--BH'
  mapagent.bhmld_ap_5.key=...
  mapagent.bhmld_ap_5.encryption='sae'
  mapagent.bhmld_ap_5.bss_index='1'
  mapagent.bhmld_ap_5.hidden='1'

With an ssid on it the placeholder then answers
agent_config_get_ap_by_ssid_on_band() for band 5, so it is reused as *the* 5 GHz
affiliated AP of the backhaul MLD and the real link is never affiliated. On that
node wlan1-1 is gone from the configuration entirely; a healthy agent has it.

What this costs downstream: re->aplist, the whole runtime AP model, is built
exclusively from 'ap' sections (agent.c:4762), and mld_parse_affiliated_ap()
pairs a link to its MLD by ap->band (mld.c:346-348). With the section gone the
link is not in the TTLM map (agent_tlv.c:4809-4826), assoc_control returns -1 on
`if (!ap || !ap->cfg)` (agent.c:6198-6200), steering cannot find the client and
num_sta does not count it.

Fix the ownership, not the sweep. map_genconfig marks its own bookkeeping
sections with 'option placeholder 1' - it is the producer, so it is the one that
knows - and map-agent skips them at the two places that raise ap->torndown. That
covers both deletion routes at their single common cause rather than adding a
predicate to each of the two sweepers, and it leaves the sweepers doing exactly
what they should: a section the controller genuinely stopped sending is still
anonymous, still unmarked, still marked torndown and still deleted. Only
sections whose producer has declared them non-provisionable are exempt, and
map_genconfig rewrites those on every boot anyway, so exempting them costs
nothing even if one were stale.

The candidate-selection sites get the same guard rather than relying on the
teardown guard alone, because agent_init_interfaces() raises ap->torndown for
the duration of a refresh cycle too, and since 970 that cycle is asynchronous.
Two of them are reachable without any torndown flag at all: the "expected_id /
unaffiliated" loop in mlo_process_ap_mld_config() matches on multi_ap and
mld_id, and a placeholder is backhaul type carrying the local backhaul mld_id -
it matches both.

The sweep itself gets the guard too, at wifi_clean_torndown_ifaces() and
wifi_clean_torndown_ifaces_on_radio(). On the paths known today that is
unreachable - the two places that raise the flag already skip placeholders - so
it is a second line rather than the fix. It is there because ap->torndown is
raised wholesale in agent_init_interfaces() as well, for the duration of a
refresh cycle that has been asynchronous since 970, and that is the one function
where the deletion is actually carried out.

Not fixed here, deliberately: clean_stale_ifaces does not run "wifi reload", so
a deletion is invisible to hostapd until something else reloads. That is a
separate matter and it should stay separate. Since 989 map-agent does not own a
wireless section for an MLD-affiliated link at all, so there is nothing for a
reload to apply on this hardware; the agent has its own reload_scheduler and
AGENT_RECONFIG_REASON_* path for what it does own; and a reload inside a
per-interface cleanup that runs in a loop would restart every BSS on the box
once per removed section - the deauth/reassoc storm 979 argues against. The
right fix for the divergence is that these sections stop being deleted, which is
this patch.

How to tell this worked, on hardware: after a sysupgrade of the controller,

  uci show mapagent | grep bhmld_ap_

must list bhmld_ap_5 and bhmld_ap_6 with type, device, ifname, band, mld_id and
placeholder - and with no ssid, key, encryption, bss_index or hidden - while
`uci show mapagent | grep -c "ifname='wlan1-1'"` returns 1. If instead a
placeholder carries an ssid again, the claim is coming from a selection site
this patch did not cover.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/config.h
+++ b/src/config.h
@@ -120,6 +120,15 @@
 	bool enabled;
 	bool sta_steer_enabled;
 	bool assoc_control;
+	/** Locally owned bookkeeping section, never a BSS the controller
+	 *  provisions. Set from 'option placeholder' which map_genconfig writes
+	 *  on the bhmld_ap_<band> sections: they exist so that apmld_parse()
+	 *  runs for the backhaul AP-MLD and they name an interface that is
+	 *  deliberately not a netdev. The controller never sends them in an M2,
+	 *  so the mark-and-sweep in the autoconfiguration path would delete
+	 *  them on every WSC M2 - see wifi_teardown_map_ifaces_by_radio().
+	 */
+	bool placeholder;
 #if (EASYMESH_VERSION > 2)
 	bool advertise_cce;
 #endif
--- a/src/config.c
+++ b/src/config.c
@@ -3192,6 +3192,7 @@
 		AP_TYPE,
 		AP_BSTA_DISALLOW,
 		AP_DISALLOW_ASSOC,
+		AP_PLACEHOLDER,
 #if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
 		AP_MLD_ID,
 		AP_HIDDEN,
@@ -3215,6 +3216,7 @@
 		[AP_TYPE] = { .name = "type", .type = UCI_TYPE_STRING },
 		[AP_BSTA_DISALLOW] = { .name = "disallow_bsta_profile", .type = UCI_TYPE_LIST },
 		[AP_DISALLOW_ASSOC] = { .name = "disallow_assoc", .type = UCI_TYPE_STRING },
+		[AP_PLACEHOLDER] = { .name = "placeholder", .type = UCI_TYPE_STRING },
 #if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
 		[AP_MLD_ID] = { .name = "mld_id", .type = UCI_TYPE_STRING },
 		[AP_HIDDEN] = { .name = "hidden", .type = UCI_TYPE_STRING },
@@ -3371,6 +3373,14 @@
 	if (tb[AP_DISALLOW_ASSOC])
 		ap->disallow_assoc = atoi(tb[AP_DISALLOW_ASSOC]->v.string);
 
+	/* Who owns this section. Default false: every section map-agent itself
+	 * writes through uci_apply_wps_credentials() is controller-provisioned
+	 * and stays subject to the ordinary teardown sweep. Only map_genconfig
+	 * sets the option, and only on its bhmld_ap_<band> bookkeeping sections.
+	 */
+	if (tb[AP_PLACEHOLDER])
+		ap->placeholder = !!atoi(tb[AP_PLACEHOLDER]->v.string);
+
 #if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
 	if (tb[AP_MLD_ID])
 		ap->mld_id = atoi(tb[AP_MLD_ID]->v.string);
--- a/src/agent_map.c
+++ b/src/agent_map.c
@@ -1788,6 +1788,18 @@
 		if (strncmp(apcfg->device, device, sizeof(apcfg->device) - 1))
 			continue;
 
+		/* A locally owned bookkeeping section is not the controller's
+		 * to tear down. This sweep marks every 'ap' section on the
+		 * radio and relies on the M2 loop below to clear the mark on
+		 * the ones the controller re-sent; the bhmld_ap_<band>
+		 * placeholders are never sent in an M2 - they exist only so
+		 * that apmld_parse() runs for the backhaul AP-MLD - so the
+		 * mark always survives and wifi_clean_torndown_ifaces_on_radio()
+		 * deletes them through 'multiap clean_stale_ifaces'.
+		 */
+		if (apcfg->placeholder)
+			continue;
+
 		wifi_teardown_iface(apcfg->name);
 		ap = agent_get_ap_by_ifname(a, apcfg->name);
 		if (ap)
@@ -1901,6 +1913,12 @@
 		if (!ap->cfg)
 			continue;
 
+		/* Never hand controller credentials to a locally owned
+		 * bookkeeping section - see wifi_get_first_available_ifname().
+		 */
+		if (ap->cfg->placeholder)
+			continue;
+
 		if (strncmp(ap->cfg->ssid, ssid, 32))
 			continue;
 
@@ -1920,6 +1938,26 @@
 		if (!ap->torndown)
 			continue;
 
+		/* A locally owned bookkeeping section is not a free BSS slot.
+		 *
+		 * Measured on the controller 2026-09-04: radio1 had no legacy
+		 * backhaul section left, so the backhaul M2 fell through to
+		 * this function, got bhmld_ap_5 - which had just been marked
+		 * torndown by wifi_teardown_map_ifaces_by_radio() - and wrote
+		 * ssid='MAP--BH', key, encryption='sae', bss_index='1' and
+		 * hidden='1' into it. The placeholder then answered
+		 * agent_config_get_ap_by_ssid_on_band() for band 5, so the
+		 * real 5 GHz backhaul link was never affiliated and wlan1-1
+		 * was gone from the configuration altogether.
+		 *
+		 * The teardown guard above already keeps placeholders out of
+		 * the torndown set; this check stands on its own because
+		 * agent_init_interfaces() also raises ap->torndown for the
+		 * duration of an (asynchronous, see 970) refresh cycle.
+		 */
+		if (ap->cfg && ap->cfg->placeholder)
+			continue;
+
 		strncpy(ifname, ap->ifname, IFNAMSIZ - 1);
 		return ap;
 	}
@@ -2214,6 +2252,20 @@
 
 	/* 1: mark affiliated APs as torndown; keep mld_id as a hint for step 2 */
 	list_for_each_entry(apcfg, &a->cfg.aplist, list) {
+		/* Second, independent route to the same deletion, and the one
+		 * that fires even when no WSC M2 is involved: this marks every
+		 * 'ap' section that carries an mld_id, and the bhmld_ap_<band>
+		 * placeholders carry mld_id='3' by construction - that is the
+		 * whole reason they exist. The controller has no MLD 3 to send
+		 * back, so step 2 never clears the mark and
+		 * wifi_clean_torndown_ifaces() at the end of this function
+		 * deletes them. The local backhaul MLD is owned by
+		 * map_genconfig, exactly as 978 and 979 established for the
+		 * mld sections themselves.
+		 */
+		if (apcfg->placeholder)
+			continue;
+
 		if (apcfg->mld_id) {
 			struct netif_ap *ap;
 
@@ -2316,6 +2368,9 @@
 					list_for_each_entry(existing, &re->aplist, list) {
 						if (!existing->cfg)
 							continue;
+						/* not a provisionable BSS */
+						if (existing->cfg->placeholder)
+							continue;
 						if (!strcmp(existing->cfg->ssid,
 							    (char *)ssid)) {
 							ap = existing;
@@ -2331,7 +2386,15 @@
 
 					list_for_each_entry(existing,
 							    &re->aplist, list) {
+						/* A placeholder is backhaul type
+						 * and already carries the local
+						 * backhaul mld_id, so it matches
+						 * both tests below and would be
+						 * handed the credentials. It is
+						 * not a BSS - skip it.
+						 */
 						if (!existing->cfg ||
+						    existing->cfg->placeholder ||
 						    existing->cfg->multi_ap !=
 						    apcfg->multi_ap)
 							continue;
--- a/src/agent.c
+++ b/src/agent.c
@@ -5473,6 +5473,26 @@
 		if (!ap->torndown)
 			continue;
 
+		/* The last stop before the uci delete.
+		 *
+		 * wifi_clean_iface() runs "multiap clean_stale_ifaces <ifname>",
+		 * which deletes every mapagent 'ap' section carrying that name
+		 * (script/multiap:927). The claim being acted on is "the
+		 * controller stopped sending this one", and that claim can only
+		 * be made about a section the controller provisions at all.
+		 *
+		 * The two places that raise the flag already skip placeholders,
+		 * so on the paths known today this is unreachable - it is a
+		 * second line, not the fix. It is here because ap->torndown is
+		 * also raised wholesale in agent_init_interfaces() for the
+		 * duration of a refresh cycle, and since 970 that cycle is
+		 * asynchronous: a path that leaves the flag set on a placeholder
+		 * arrives here, at the one place where the deletion is actually
+		 * carried out. Cheap to hold the line at the gate as well.
+		 */
+		if (ap->cfg && ap->cfg->placeholder)
+			continue;
+
 		wifi_clean_iface(ap->ifname);
 		clean_ap(ap->cfg);
 		netif_free(ap);
@@ -5492,6 +5512,9 @@
 		list_for_each_entry_safe(ap, ap_tmp, &re->aplist, list) {
 			if (!ap->torndown)
 				continue;
+			/* see wifi_clean_torndown_ifaces_on_radio() */
+			if (ap->cfg && ap->cfg->placeholder)
+				continue;
 			wifi_clean_iface(ap->ifname);
 			clean_ap(ap->cfg);
 			netif_free(ap);
